(Sun Tzu said: The art of war is of vital importance to the State. It is a) Tj
72 9786 Td
(matter of life and death, a road either to safety or to ruin. Hence it is a) Tj
72 9772 Td
(subject of inquiry which can on no account be neglected.

The art of war,) Tj
72 9758 Td
(then, is governed by five constant factors, to be taken into account in) Tj
72 9744 Td
(one's deliberations, when seeking to determine the conditions obtaining in) Tj
72 9730 Td
(the field. These are: The Moral Law; Heaven; Earth; The Commander; Method) Tj
72 9716 Td
(and discipline.

The Moral Law causes the people to be in complete accord) Tj
72 9702 Td
(with their ruler, so that they will follow him regardless of their lives,) Tj
72 9688 Td
(undismayed by any danger.

All warfare is based on deception. Hence, when) Tj
72 9674 Td
(able to attack, we must seem unable; when using our forces, we must seem) Tj
72 9660 Td
(inactive.) Tj
