/F1 12 Tf
72 9800 Td
(In the practical art of war, the best thing of all is to take the enemy's) Tj
72 9786 Td
(country whole and intact; to shatter and destroy it is not so good. So,) Tj
72 9772 Td
(too, it is better to recruit an army than to destroy an army.

Where the) Tj
72 9758 Td
(army is, prices are high; when prices rise the wealth of the State is) Tj
72 9744 Td
(exhausted. When wealth is exhausted, the peasantry will be afflicted by) Tj
72 9730 Td
(heavy exactions. The stressed troops will lose heart, and the army will) Tj
72 9716 Td
(crumble.

Thus, though we have heard of stupid haste in war, cleverness has) Tj
72 9702 Td
(never been seen associated with long delays. There is no instance of a) Tj
72 9688 Td
(country having benefited from prolonged warfare.) Tj
