BT
/F1 12 Tf
72 9800 Td
(In the practical art of war, the best thing of all is to take the enemy's) Tj
72 9786 Td
(country whole and intact; to shatter and destroy it is not so) Tj
72 9772 Td
(good.

Supreme excellence consists of breaking the enemy's resistance) Tj
72 9758 Td
(without fighting. Thus the highest form of generalship is to balk the) Tj
72 9744 Td
(enemy's plans; the next best is to prevent the junction of the enemy's) Tj
72 9730 Td
(forces; the next in order is to attack the enemy's army in the field; and) Tj
72 9716 Td
(the worst policy of all is to besiege walled cities.

Hence the skillful) Tj
72 9702 Td
(fighter puts himself into a position which makes defeat impossible, and) Tj
72 9688 Td
(does not miss the moment for defeating the enemy.) Tj
